    "question": "You notice that when the same Claude Code session that generated a change also reviews it, the review is conspicuously gentle — missing issues an independent reviewer catches. Why, and what is the design implication?",
    "options": {
      "A": "The model is being polite; instruct it to be harsher",
      "B": "Reviews should always be performed by a larger model tier than the one that generated the change",
      "C": "A session keeps the reasoning that produced the code, biasing it toward its own decisions — review independently",
      "D": "Reviews should run at temperature zero so the reviewer applies its standards consistently across findings"
    },
