    "explanation": "Consistency comes from operational definitions: severity levels anchored by concrete examples give the classifier something to match, turning a vibe into a rubric. That is what makes severity gates dependable. Why not the others: B discards the signal the merge gate needs; C reduces run-to-run noise but leaves the judgment unanchored — majority votes over a vibe are still a vibe; D measures size, not impact — a one-line auth bypass outranks a fifty-line comment tweak.",
