    "explanation": "The least-privilege principle dictates that each subagent should only have access to the tools it genuinely needs. In a multi-agent system this is critical because a compromised or prompt-injected subagent with broad tool access could cause far greater damage than one with narrowly scoped tools. The `allowed_tools` parameter enforces this deterministically.",
