    "explanation": "The correct approach is a validate-and-retry loop: extract the generated test code, run a lightweight syntax check, and if validation fails, re-invoke Claude Code with the original prompt plus the syntax error as additional context. This self-correction pattern is idiomatic for LLM pipelines and leverages Claude's ability to fix its own output when given explicit error feedback.",
