    "id": "C-q-3.6-hard-4",
    "scenario": "A team runs Claude Code in CI to both review code and generate tests. They observe that the review step occasionally posts duplicate comments on a PR when the workflow is re-triggered by a new commit push before the previous run finishes. The duplicate comments come from two concurrent workflow runs both completing successfully.",
    "domain": "Claude Code Configuration & Workflows",
    "task": "3.6",
    "taskTitle": "Integrate Claude Code into CI/CD pipelines",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "type": "single",
    "select": 1,
    "question": "Which solution BEST addresses duplicate output from concurrent Claude Code CI runs without sacrificing review coverage?",
    "options": {
      "A": "Add `concurrency: group: pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}, cancel-in-progress: true` to the workflow to cancel superseded runs",
      "B": "Add an idempotency check in the Claude Code prompt: include a unique run ID and instruct Claude to skip if already reviewed",
      "C": "Use `--output-format json` and parse the response to detect if identical output was already posted before submitting the PR comment",
      "D": "Add a `sleep 30` between the review and comment steps to ensure only one workflow run reaches the comment step"
    },
    "correct": [
      "A"
    ],
    "explanation": "GitHub Actions' `concurrency` key with `cancel-in-progress: true` cancels any in-progress run for the same PR when a new commit is pushed, ensuring only the latest run completes and posts results. This is the idiomatic GitHub Actions solution: it prevents duplicate runs at the platform level without requiring application-level deduplication logic.",
    "whyWrong": {
      "B": "Instructing Claude Code via prompt to 'skip if already reviewed' is unreliable because Claude Code is stateless and has no knowledge of prior CI runs. This would require additional external state management and does not leverage the platform's built-in concurrency controls.",
      "C": "Comparing output content to detect duplicates requires reading existing PR comments and adding complex deduplication logic. This is fragile (minor wording differences would fail the check) and far more complex than the platform-native `concurrency` solution.",
      "D": "Adding `sleep 30` is a race condition anti-pattern. It does not guarantee serialization and wastes CI time. The `concurrency` key provides deterministic, race-free run management."
    },
    "refs": [
      "https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/github-actions",
      "https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-jobs/using-concurrency"
    ],
