    "id": "C-q-4.2-hard-3",
    "scenario": "An engineer is using few-shot prompting to build a content moderation system. She crafts eight examples: six showing acceptable content with the label 'ALLOW' and two showing clearly harmful content with the label 'BLOCK'. During A/B testing, the system has high recall for obvious violations but a 40% false-negative rate on subtle policy violations — content that is technically borderline but should be blocked per company policy.",
