    "question": "What is the most likely root cause of Claude repeating the same erroneous value, and how should the error message be improved?",
    "options": {
      "A": "The model's context window is too small; increase max_tokens",
      "B": "The error message lacked actionable guidance; it should state the conflicting value and suggest a corrective action such as checking for an existing record",
      "C": "The retry logic is firing too quickly; add a delay",
      "D": "The tool schema is missing a description field; add one"
    },
    "correct": [
      "B"
    ],
    "explanation": "Claude adjusts behaviour based on the content of the error message. If the message only names the constraint without indicating what the model should do differently (e.g., look up the existing record or generate a new ID), Claude has insufficient signal to change its approach.",
    "whyWrong": {
      "A": "Context window size does not explain why Claude repeats the same value; the error message is already in context.",
      "C": "A timing delay does not change the information available to Claude and would not prevent repeating the same value.",
      "D": "Adding a description to the tool schema helps with initial parameter selection but does not address how Claude interprets runtime errors."
    },
