    "explanation": "Accuracy tracking by document type should inform where review effort goes. Contracts have a 22% error rate — more than double the invoice rate — so they deserve a disproportionately large share of the review budget. However, completely ignoring invoices and purchase orders leaves blind spots. The correct approach is accuracy-weighted allocation: more reviews where accuracy is lowest, but some baseline coverage of every document type. This is distinct from simple proportional (volume-based) allocation which ignores accuracy differences.",
