    "explanation": "When accuracy drops on a specific field type after a model change but confidence scores remain unchanged, it signals a calibration regression: the model's self-reported confidence no longer tracks actual performance for that field. Accuracy tracking by document type and field type is precisely designed to catch this pattern. The immediate response is to lower the auto-approve threshold for contract date fields (routing more to human review) and investigate the model update for a regression in date parsing, with retraining or rollback as remediation.",
